{"id":"u-16895c28-4a31-4102-8f2a-8910a105ace6","src":"community","title":"Chest Focus PPL | 6-Day Hypertrophy","author":"Maxime S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/al62rz-chest-focus-ppl-or-6-day-hypertrophy-1","desc":"A 12-week, 6-day push/pull/legs (PPL) hypertrophy program with an emphasis on chest development.\n\nDesigned for intermediate lifters who enjoy training frequently and have access to a fully equipped gym.\n\nTHE SPLIT\n• Day 1 — Push 1\n• Day 2 — Pull 1\n• Day 3 — Legs 1\n• Day 4 — Push 2\n• Day 5 — Pull 2\n• Day 6 — Legs 2\n\nCHEST EMPHASIS\nBoth push sessions begin with a cable chest isolation exercise before moving into presses. Flat and incline pressing variations, cable flyes and pec deck work provide the chest emphasis, alongside direct shoulder and triceps training.\n\nBACK AND ARMS\nPull sessions combine vertical pulls, supported rows and unilateral rows with direct biceps, rear-delt and upper-back work.\n\nLOWER BODY\nThe two leg sessions include hack squats, barbell squats, Romanian deadlifts, leg curls, leg extensions, hip thrusts and calf raises.\n\nPROGRAM AT A GLANCE\n• Goal: muscle growth / hypertrophy\n• Length: 12 weeks\n• Frequency: 6 workouts per week\n• Session length: approximately 70 minutes, depending on the workout and rest periods\n• Equipment: barbells, dumbbells, cables, Smith machine and gym machines\n• Experience: intermediate\n\nPROGRESSION\nFollow the sets, rep ranges and any RPE targets listed for each exercise. Aim to increase your repetitions and/or weight each week while maintaining consistent technique and respecting the prescribed effort level.\n\nBuild up your repetitions within the listed range. Once you reach the top of that range across all prescribed sets with consistent form, increase the weight by the smallest practical increment and work back up from the lower end of the range.\n\nSTANDARDIZE YOUR REPS\nMake every repetition comparable: use the same setup, range of motion and controlled tempo each session. Keep rest periods consistent when comparing performances.\n\nDo not shorten the movement, bounce or add momentum just to lift more weight or complete extra reps. Progress means doing more under the same conditions.\n\nLog your weights and repetitions after each session. If you cannot improve without changing your technique or exceeding the target effort, repeat the same load and aim to progress next time.\n\nThis is my personal training routine, shared for lifters looking for a structured PPL with extra attention to chest development.\n\nHave fun, and feel free to give me feedback.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-09-30T17:05:13.475Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push 1","Pull 1","Legs 1","Push 2","Pull 2","Legs 2"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Cable Crossover","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":4,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Magic Triceps Dumbbell","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Military Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bayesian Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Pec Deck","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug (Chest Supported)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x"